    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0535" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg503"/>

                <head>282. Telegram From the Embassy in Jordan to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d282-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Amman</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-08-20T23:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                                1958—11 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>581. USUN for Rountree. Reference: Embtel 564 repeated information USUN
                        16.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d282-f2"/> King Hussein has sent me word [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>]
                    that Prime Minister Rifai has informed him intention resign as outlined
                    reference telegram. According Hussein Rifai set August 30 as deadline receipt
                    USG reply. If none received by that time indicated he would resign shortly
                    thereafter. Significant in his conversation with me yesterday Rifai made no such
                    stipulation.</p>
                <p>Hussein said unless USG comes forward promptly commitment provide
                    military/economic assistance including large scale budgetary aid which will
                    assure Jordan adequate support not “for a week or a month but for at least two
                    years” he about reached conclusion pro-western policies present HKJ government
                    futile. His opinion when/as/if government changed there can be no half-way
                    measures. Circumstances will dictate new government must be completely
                    pro-Nasser/UAR.</p>
                <pb facs="0536" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>
                <p>King said under present circumstances has moral obligation Hashemite dynasty as
                    well those loyal supporters whose lives and fortunes like his own are now placed
                    in jeopardy. [<hi rendition="#italic">7 lines of source text not
                        declassified</hi>]</p>
                <p>“In response query as to his personal plans King replied has not yet made up his
                    mind but said he not interested building in any brakes once decision made change
                    government.”</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi> Quite evident both Hussein/RIFAI have
                    within last few days come conclusion only American miracle can save Jordan [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5½ lines of source text not declassified</hi>].</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#bold">Wright</hi></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
